{"seconds": 31.9, "exit": 0, "final": "Qc7+ is check but not mate. Qxa8+ wins the rook. Either way, White is decisively winning. The main motif is a **fork** (and then a deflection/attraction of the king).\n\n---\n\n**Coaching Note:**\n\nYour queen on f7 was perfectly placed to fork the king and pawn on e6. When Black's pawn advanced, it set up this tactic. Qxe6+ forces the king away, and after Kc7 (the only try), Qxc6+ wins material and dominates. Always scan your queen's lines for undefended pieces the opponent's king must protect\u2014that's often where a fork lies.\n\n---\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxe6+\", \"line\": [\"Qxe6+\", \"Kc7\", \"Qxc6+\", \"Kb8\", \"Qxa8+\", \"Qxa8\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\", \"attraction\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "square": "a5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "square": "e4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "square": "h4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "square": "f7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "move": "Qxe6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1p/2pkp3/q1ppp3/4nP1b/1P2P3/P1PPK1PP/RN5R w - - 0 18", "move": "fxe5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r5r1/p4Q1